    <string name="timeline_help_sky_title">Sky and precipitation</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_sky">The yellow glow shows daylight and clearer sky, the gray layer shows cloud cover, and the crescent marks night. Blue drops mean rain, snowflakes mean snow, and diamonds mean hail.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_temperature_title">Temperature</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_temperature">The colored line is air temperature. Its color follows your temperature thresholds. The shaded ribbon can show feels-like temperature.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_wind_title">Wind</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_wind">Flowing lines show wind speed over time. Taller, denser waves mean stronger wind. Direction arrows are shown when enabled.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_uv_title">UV index</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_uv">The violet intensity strip follows the UV index: faint means low exposure and vivid means stronger exposure.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_humidity_title">Humidity</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_humidity">Blue droplets form a denser cloud as relative humidity rises.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_pressure_title">Atmospheric pressure</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_pressure">The ribbon thickens near pressure extremes. Red with H marks pressure above the local average, blue with L marks pressure below it, and the thin center shows values near the average.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_air_quality_title">Air quality</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_air_quality">Gray particles become denser as the European Air Quality Index rises. Lower values are better.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_pollen_title">Pollen</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_pollen">Colored pollen grains become denser as the combined hourly pollen concentration rises.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_mushrooms_title">Mushroom conditions</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_mushrooms">This band combines recent rain, humidity and soil moisture into an estimate of mushroom-growing conditions.</string>
